# Dark mode

- Source of truth: `fixtures/tokens/mapping.json` (`dark` + `brand.dark`) → `bun run tokens` → `packages/tokens/theme.css` (light: `:root, [data-theme="light"]`, dark: `.dark, [data-theme="dark"]`) and each app's `brand.css` (brand colors only). Never hand-edit emitted CSS.
- Variant: `@custom-variant dark (&:where(.dark, .dark *))` lives in packages/tokens. `dark:` matches the `.dark` class only, **not** `[data-theme="dark"]` — inside a data-theme scope rely on tokens, not `dark:` utilities.
- Prefer tokens over `dark:`: a token that flips (bg-card, text-foreground…) needs no variant. `dark:` is for non-token effects (`dark:brightness-0 dark:invert` on raster logos).
- Pastel/brand tiles that carry foreground text need **deep** dark tones (chart-3/4/5 dark = #5b4660/#1e3a5f/#5c2b33), never the light pastel under white text. Check contrast (≥ 4.5:1 body text) in `bun run shots:modes` output.
- `data-theme="light"` forces a light island (hero on orange stays light in dark mode); `data-theme="dark"` forces a dark island (Premium plan, footer newsletter panel). Never use `data-theme` values `light`/`dark` as plain variant keys — a variant key named `light` silently forces light tokens (pricing plan bug, fixed by naming it `default`).
- No-flash: `packages/ui/behaviors/theme-init.js` is the **only inline script** allowed. Site: `views/layout.templ` `themeInit` (templ.Raw, passed via `-theme-init`). Design app: `%theme-init%` in `app.html`, replaced in `hooks.server.ts`. It reads `localStorage.theme`, else `prefers-color-scheme`, and toggles `.dark` on `<html>`. Never set `style`/`colorScheme` from JS — `scheme-light`/`scheme-dark` live in adapter base.css.
- Toggle: the `ThemeToggle` primitive (codegen 2.0 spec `themetoggle.json`, `data-ui8kit="theme-toggle"`, `aria-pressed`, Lucide sun/moon). Behaviour is only in `packages/ui/behaviors/ui8kit.js` (persists `localStorage.theme`, follows OS changes until the user chooses).
- Every new block/page: verify both modes (`bun run shots:modes`, `bun run test:behaviors`).
